# Component Standards

- Reuse existing primitives from `components/ui/` before introducing new base components.
- Keep components small and focused; extract reusable logic to hooks when needed.
- Match naming, prop structure, and styling patterns already used in neighboring files.

# Accessibility and UX

- Preserve keyboard accessibility and semantic HTML.
- Keep visual and interaction behavior consistent with current UI patterns.
- Avoid introducing custom behavior that duplicates existing shared components.

# Type Safety

- Use explicit TypeScript props and domain types from `types/`.
- Avoid `any`; prefer narrow unions and existing interfaces.
